{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++17 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++17 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nusing ll = long long;\n\nconst ll MOD = 1000000007LL;\n\nclass Solver {\n    ll n, k;\n    vector<char> used;\n    vector<ll> freq, weight;\n\n    ll binpow(ll a, ll e) {\n        if (e < 0) e = -e;\n        a %= MOD;\n        ll r = 1;\n        while (e) {\n            if (e & 1) r = r * a % MOD;\n            a = a * a % MOD;\n            e >>= 1;\n        }\n        return r;\n    }\n\n    ll journey(ll start) {\n        ll cur = start;\n        ll length = 0;\n        while (!used[cur]) {\n            used[cur] = 1;\n            cur = (cur * k) % n;\n            ++length;\n        }\n        return length;\n    }\n\npublic:\n    Solver(ll n_, ll k_) : n(n_), k(k_), used(n_, 0), freq(n_ + 1, 0), weight(n_ + 1, 0) {}\n\n    ll solve() {\n        if (k == 0) return binpow(n, n - 1);\n\n        for (ll i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n            if (!used[i]) {\n                ++freq[journey(i)];\n            }\n        }\n\n        for (ll len = 1; len <= n; ++len) {\n            if (freq[len] == 0) continue;\n            ll add = len * freq[len];\n            for (ll multiple = len; multiple <= n; multiple += len) {\n                if (freq[multiple]) weight[multiple] += add;\n            }\n        }\n\n        ll ans = 1;\n        for (ll i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {\n            if (freq[i]) ans = ans * binpow(weight[i], freq[i]) % MOD;\n        }\n        return ans;\n    }\n};\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    ll n, k;\n    cin >> n >> k;\n\n    Solver solver(n, k);\n    cout << solver.solve() << '\\n';\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.Scanner;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static final long MOD = 1000000007L;\n\n    static class Solver {\n        long n, k;\n        boolean[] used;\n        long[] freq, weight;\n\n        Solver(long n_, long k_) {\n            n = n_;\n            k = k_;\n            used = new boolean[(int)n];\n            freq = new long[(int)n + 1];\n            weight = new long[(int)n + 1];\n        }\n\n        long binpow(long a, long e) {\n            if (e < 0) e = -e;\n            a %= MOD;\n            long r = 1;\n            while (e > 0) {\n                if ((e & 1) == 1) r = r * a % MOD;\n                a = a * a % MOD;\n                e >>= 1;\n            }\n            return r;\n        }\n\n        long journey(long start) {\n            long cur = start;\n            long length = 0;\n            while (!used[(int)cur]) {\n                used[(int)cur] = true;\n                cur = (cur * k) % n;\n                ++length;\n            }\n            return length;\n        }\n\n        long solve() {\n            if (k == 0) return binpow(n, n - 1);\n\n            for (long i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n                if (!used[(int)i]) {\n                    ++freq[(int)journey(i)];\n                }\n            }\n\n            for (long len = 1; len <= n; ++len) {\n                if (freq[(int)len] == 0) continue;\n                long add = len * freq[(int)len];\n                for (long multiple = len; multiple <= n; multiple += len) {\n                    if (freq[(int)multiple] != 0) weight[(int)multiple] += add;\n                }\n            }\n\n            long ans = 1;\n            for (long i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {\n                if (freq[(int)i] != 0) ans = ans * binpow(weight[(int)i], freq[(int)i]) % MOD;\n            }\n            return ans;\n        }\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long n = sc.nextLong();\n        long k = sc.nextLong();\n        Solver solver = new Solver(n, k);\n        System.out.println(solver.solve());\n        sc.close();\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.98\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -3.8265450712060556e-05, -2.861018856492592e-06, 0.0, -0.00018165845540352166, -0.03820665553212166, -0.0011723319767042994, -0.0001599660754436627, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.39479848742485046, -0.0019364668987691402, -5.8887653722194955e-05, -0.08024299889802933, -2.3841830625315197e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.0005529781919904053, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -8.344646857949556e-07, -0.001930398982949555, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.01834029145538807, -0.1002238392829895, 0.0, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -0.0001530530134914443, 0.0, -0.0003355178632773459, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -5.960462772236497e-07, -0.0005541696446016431, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.07913131266832352, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -6.246371776796877e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.0023743314668536186, 0.0, -8.344646857949556e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.4740777313709259, 0.0, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -2.264974000354414e-06, 0.0, -0.0031777145341038704, 0.0, 0.0, -